@startuml harness-functions
title Harness functions — framework user, orchestrator agent, step subagents, host, harness

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30
skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "Framework user" as User
participant "Workflow Orchestrator agent" as Orch
participant "Step subagent" as Sub
participant "Host\n(e.g. GitHub Copilot)" as Host
participant "Harness" as Harness

note over Harness
  Every function invocation appends one
  entry to the workflow-instance log
  (functions 12-13 are instance-less).
end note

== Conversation start ==
User -> Host : engage a facilitator agent (VMO / RTE / SM)\nwith a request — a question or an intent
Host -> Harness : hook ""sessionStart"" (agent session)
Harness -> Harness : framework-agent gate (C7):\nactor resolves to a framework agent\n(else pass through, untouched and unlogged)
Harness -> Harness : no open dispatch — an orchestrator session:\n""7 inject-workflow-instructions"" — catalog map + return-handling instructions\n""8 inject-workflow-skills"" — selection + procedure skills
Harness --> Host : context to inject
Host --> Orch : session opens carrying the catalog map and the\n""*-handling"" instructions for every harness return

== Workflow selection (no harness call) ==
Orch -> Orch : per ""workflow-selection-handling"" instruction —\nmatch the user's intent against the injected catalog map
alt the intent maps to one workflow (the orchestrator's selection skill)
  Orch --> User : proposes it
else ambiguous or unmatched intent (optional engagement turns)
  Orch --> User : engages — answers, asks which workflow to enter
  User -> Orch : clarifies the intent
end
User -> Orch : assent — start the workflow\n(or continue one by naming its instance id)

loop until ""1 resolve-step"" resolves no-next-step

== Step resolution ==
alt opening — no instance yet (first pass)
  Orch -> Harness : ""1 resolve-step"" (workflowSlug)
  Harness -> Harness : open the instance:\nmint the workflow-instance id + create its log
else continuing — the instance is known
  Orch -> Harness : ""1 resolve-step"" (workflowSlug, workflowInstanceId)
end
Harness -> Harness : ""2 resolve-step-model"" — resolved once, here\n(capabilities × catalog → model binding)
Harness --> Orch : step resolution — configured step + model + instance\ncontext (the instance id: the orchestrator's handle)
Orch -> Orch : per ""step-resolution-handling"" instruction —\nrelay the resolution verbatim

== Step dispatch (1 step = 1 agent = 1 session = 1 artifact) ==
Orch -> Host : ""runSubagent"" (the resolution verbatim:\nactor, model, skills, instructions, prompts)
Host -> Harness : hook ""preToolUse"" dispatch (step-open)
Harness -> Harness : ""3 check-step-preconditions"" — THE enforcement point
alt preconditions hold
  Harness --> Host : allow
else a precondition fails
  Harness --> Host : deny + reports
  Host --> Orch : dispatch blocked, reports returned
  Orch -> Orch : per ""reports-handling"" instruction — produce the missing\nstate (via a prior step or the user), dispatch again
end
Host -> Sub : open the step session
Host -> Harness : hook ""sessionStart"" (step session)
Harness -> Harness : open dispatch found — a step session:\n""9 inject-step-instructions"" — the step's refs\n""10 inject-step-skills"" — the step's skills
Harness --> Host : context to inject
Host --> Sub : session carries the step's constraints

== Step work — every write guarded ==
Sub -> Host : write artifact (host write tool)
Host -> Harness : hook ""preToolUse"" write (write-open)
Harness -> Harness : ""5 check-step-authorization""
alt privilege granted
  Harness --> Host : allow
  Host -> Host : execute the write
else no grant
  Harness --> Host : deny (missing privilege)
  Host --> Sub : write blocked, report returned
  Sub -> Sub : per its step instructions — proceed without the write,\nor return it to the orchestrator (privileged-author route)
end
Host -> Harness : hook ""postToolUse"" write (write-close)
Harness -> Harness : ""6 check-step-artifacts""
alt write is schema-valid
  Harness --> Host : valid
else invalid write
  Harness -> Harness : revert (restore last-committed / delete)
  Harness --> Host : denied + schema reports
  Host --> Sub : reports returned
  Sub -> Sub : per its step instructions — rewrite per the\nschema reports and retry the write
end

== Step close ==
Sub --> Host : step session ends
Host -> Harness : hook ""postToolUse"" dispatch (step-close)
Harness -> Harness : ""4 check-step-postconditions"" — THE evaluation point:\nthe step outcome logs against the state the step left
alt postconditions hold — step journaled executed
  Harness --> Host : outcome pass
  Host --> Orch : dispatch returns — next iteration resolves the next step
else postconditions fail — step not journaled executed
  Harness --> Host : outcome fail + reports
  Host --> Orch : dispatch returns with reports
  Orch -> Orch : per ""reports-handling"" instruction — retry inside the workflow,\ninvisible to the user: the next iteration re-resolves the failed step\n(the harness governs the sequencing, not the agent)
end

end

== Workflow return ==
Orch -> Harness : ""1 resolve-step"" (workflowSlug, workflowInstanceId)
Harness --> Orch : ""no-next-step"" + advisory successors\n(a reversible observation — never "done")
Orch -> Orch : per ""no-next-step-handling"" instruction
Orch --> User : end-to-end workflow results (delivered artifacts)\n+ options: reiterate the workflow / take a successor
note right of Orch
  The user sees workflow results only —
  never intermediate step results.
  Step retries happen inside the workflow:
  re-resolution on negative reports (invariant 7).
end note

== Conversation close ==
Host -> Harness : hook ""stop"" / ""sessionEnd""
Harness -> Harness : record only — no policy at session close

== Audit & global checks (on demand — also CI-triggered) ==
Orch -> Harness : ""11 audit-workflow-instance"" (workflowInstanceId)
Harness --> Orch : audit report — every recorded write\nre-verified against the ACL
Orch -> Harness : ""12 check-workspace"" (scope)
Harness --> Orch : reports (C6 proven when empty)
Orch -> Harness : ""13 check-configuration"" (framework root)
Harness --> Orch : reports (.env layout, conf files, adapters)
note right of Harness
  CI pipelines run 12 on the workspace
  repository and 13 on the framework
  repository as merge gates.
end note

@enduml
